SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Checkmate" with Ben Mezrich
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/187622\n\n5:00PM Reception
 \, 5:30PM Discussion \nStep into the high-stakes world of Checkmate with 
 bestselling author Ben Mezrich—an electrifying true story that unravels 
 the biggest scandal in modern chess.\n\nIn September 2022\, the chess worl
 d was shaken when nineteen-year-old American prodigy Hans Niemann defeated
  reigning world champion Magnus Carlsen in a stunning upset. Days later\, 
 Carlsen accused Niemann of cheating—an allegation that ignited a global 
 firestorm\, drawing in Chess.com\, the media\, and a rapidly expanding dig
 ital audience. What followed was a dramatic collision of reputation\, riva
 lry\, and power.\n\nBut Checkmate is about far more than controversy. It�
 �s a portrait of ambition at its sharpest edge—a young player willing to
  risk everything to rise\, and a legendary figure determined to defend his
  legacy. Set against the backdrop of a centuries-old game transformed by s
 treaming\, sponsorships\, and Silicon Valley influence\, Mezrich brings re
 aders inside a world that is as cutthroat as it is cerebral.\n\n*This even
 t is complimentary and reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshm
 ents will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/187622
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
